  "body": "Context : \n- applying rules described here https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-main-intd over acid2 test (http://acid2.acidtests.org/).\n- processing the `<p><table><tr><td></table><p class=\"bad\">` line.\n- processing the `</table>` token\n- current opened elements stack is td/tr/tbody/table/div/body/html\n- `</table>` is not in table scope (table node not current in stack and table scope contains 'table' in html namespace so returns failure)\n\nPer spec, a parser error must occur and the token must be ignored, but doing so, the table is not closed and the rest of the document is considered children of the unclosed `<td>`\n\nA proposed fix would be :\n- keep parser error (obviously)\n- if token is a `</table>` token, pop elements from the stack of open elements until a \"table\" node has been popped of the stack\n- ignore the token\n\nI hope I did not got confused somewhere :)\n",
